; Unpack N columns of a packed sprite set
;
; The packed format, per column: for each character row (8 pixel rows) one flag byte, most significant bit first; for
; each bit a set bit means that a literal byte follows in the stream and becomes the next pixel byte, a clear bit repeats
; the previous pixel byte of the column (0 at the top of a column). So a run of equal bytes costs one flag bit. Each
; pixel byte goes to the next page (INC D): pixel row 0 at the destination, row 1 in the page above, and so on; then the
; next column is the next byte of the page (INC E). Stops after N columns or when the set has no more columns
; (BC is counted down once per column, the caller's DJNZ takes the last one of a frame).
;
; A Frame width N: columns to unpack in this call
; B Columns of the set left to unpack
; C Character rows of the set
; HL Packed stream, at a flag byte
; DE Destination: D = page of pixel row 0, E = column
; O:A N
; O:B Columns left, less N - 1 (1 when the set ran out first)
; O:HL Packed stream after the columns
; O:DE Destination of the next column (E + N)
@label=UnpackColumns
c$AF58 PUSH AF       ; N
@label=UnpackColumns_Column
*$AF59 PUSH BC       ;
 $AF5A PUSH DE       ;
 $AF5B PUSH AF       ;
 $AF5C XOR A         ; the pixel byte "so far" is 0 at the top of a column
@label=UnpackColumns_Row
*$AF5D LD B,(HL)     ; flag byte of a character row
 $AF5E INC HL        ;
 $AF5F SCF           ;
 $AF60 RL B          ; carry = first flag bit, a marker bit enters at the bottom to end the loop after 8 bits
*$AF62 JR NC,$AF66   ; clear: repeat the previous byte
 $AF64 LD A,(HL)     ; set: a literal byte
 $AF65 INC HL        ;
*$AF66 LD (DE),A     ;
 $AF67 INC D         ; next pixel row
 $AF68 SLA B         ;
 $AF6A JR NZ,$AF62   ;
 $AF6C DEC C         ;
 $AF6D JR NZ,$AF5D   ; next character row
 $AF6F POP AF        ;
 $AF70 POP DE        ;
 $AF71 POP BC        ;
 $AF72 INC E         ; next column
 $AF73 DEC A         ;
 $AF74 JR Z,$AF79    ; N columns done
 $AF76 DJNZ $AF59    ; more columns in the set
 $AF78 INC B         ; the set ran out: B = 1 for the caller's DJNZ
*$AF79 POP AF        ;
 $AF7A RET           ;
